30,2,,status,Takumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
31,2,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,Jonathan,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Asuka,,The taster forms are clear. Nine out of fourteen said they wouldn't commit to a whole year at once.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,The treasurer's logs are brutal. Chasing individual payments took six hours a month. A yearly collection took one.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,The sign-in sheets show a quarter of members do two-thirds of the work. Eighteen people never signed in.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,The winter social feedback confirms it. Quiet members feel uneasy about the cost per visit.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Takumi,,The ledger shows seventy percent of costs are fixed. Hall hire and insurance don't care if anyone comes.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Benjamin, if we charge per event, the admin load will explode.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Asuka, yes. The data proves it. We need a system that minimizes chasing.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Takumi, if costs are fixed, a flat fee makes sense for the core, but what about the non-attendees?","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Jonathan, the non-attendees are the ones feeling the pressure. They don't want to pay for what they don't use.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Shunichi, but if we don't charge them, the core members subsidize them. Is that fair?","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"We need a middle ground. A base fee for the fixed costs, but something that doesn't scare off the drifters.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"A tiered system might work. A low base for access, and higher tiers for heavy users.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,But the minute books from the last time we tried grades show friction. People stopped putting themselves forward.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Jonathan, that is a risk. But the current hesitation is worse.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Takumi,,I am worried about the bank statements. A third of renewals needed reminders. We need simplicity.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Asuka,,Let's look at the options. We have to balance admin ease with fairness.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"Option B, Tiered Membership, seems to address the admin load while allowing choice.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,I am hesitant. The friction from the past is a warning.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,But the quiet members need a way in that doesn't feel like a big commitment.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Takumi,,I will support whatever reduces the chasing. I am tired of guessing.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,,status,Takumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
56,3,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
57,3,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
58,3,,status,Jonathan,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
59,3,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"Option A is flat. Simple, but ignores the uneven usage.","{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,Option B is tiered. It allows people to choose their level of commitment.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"Option C is activity-based. It is fair, but the admin nightmare is real.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,I lean towards B. It gives the quiet members a low entry point.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Takumi,,I am concerned about the reminders. B might still require chasing if tiers are complex.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Benjamin, how do we handle the mid-year joiners in a tiered system?","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Asuka, we can pro-rate the tier fee. It is less work than calculating individual event costs.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shunichi, do you think the quiet members will actually choose the lower tier?","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Jonathan, yes. They are uneasy about the cost. A lower tier validates their presence.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Takumi,,I need to know if the fixed costs are covered by the base tier.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Asuka,,The ledger shows fixed costs are high. The base tier must be enough to cover that.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"If the base tier covers the fixed costs, the higher tiers are for the extras.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,That sounds reasonable. It protects the core while allowing flexibility.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,It also reduces the social pressure. You are paying for what you choose.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Takumi,,I can live with that. It is better than guessing.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Asuka,,I am ready to vote.,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,I am ready.,"{""words"":3,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,"I am ready, though I remain cautious.","{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,I am ready.,"{""words"":3,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Takumi,,I am ready.,"{""words"":3,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
